    "body": "Remove the global runner dependency from start-agent-session and inject a validated runtime-owned spawn capability through the actor context. Missing/nonfunction values refuse before contract resolution or runner admission; caller/payload capability data cannot replace the trusted function. Both captured Discord message and voice callbacks now receive that capability as well as the normal event/HTTP ingress paths. invoke-agent, runner implementation/payloads and internal/external event provenance remain unchanged.\n\nThis24-file implementation/card/event diff follows two complete evidence layers144/17files. Final headc46f571ba70d155fcd62080a9eec0831f5101f96 has the exact complete tree5fc52d73de5ca64c4addc90253678803a373636e of tested frozen9faf, preserved through an ordinary evidence merge. Independent peer found no further actionable source defect after the Discord repair; that is local inspection, not native approving review. All2,580 other inherited entries and three ledger/reflection prefixes remain intact.\n\nValidation: guarded full compiled suite1854tests/9152assertions/0failures/0errors/process0 and zero compilewarnings; production server typecheck0warnings/process0; boundarycheckPASS; unchanged JS75/75. Corrected predecessor and Discord gateway RED are retained; earlier malformed-stub RED is unqualified. The real private HTTP401/202 smoke crosses production dispatch/action/runner and durableClio run/thread admission plus a local active agent session. Authentication, provider creation, hydration and prompting use explicit local seams, so the runnable script/docs pair establishes isolated automated smoke and does not finish whole-live-application manual acceptance. Both Discord callbacks are exercised without a gateway connection.\n\nNative only161 Ready\u2192Todo\u2192InProgress and exactly one HOLD comment are retained. Directblocked was rejected even though the process exited0; actual card staysin_progress with original criteria/UUID/3points preserved. No checklist completion is claimed.\n\nAll original issue161 acceptance remains in scope. Required lint exits3 with8errors/288warnings, matching the accepted diagnostic baseline under existing owners181/182; it is not waived. The required whole live-Knoxx authenticated trigger/session manual smoke remains unverified. Parent syncPR1 is draft and unqualified, so this is a blocked draft later layer with automatic merge off. No review request, native approval, completed cohort, merge, live-service restart, deployed authentication or paid provider qualification is supplied. Development stays on the personal fork; final release/deploy integration into origin requires qualified exact evidence.\n\nThe whole preserved candidate is9faf559120aa345777a2c2ef5edc52e560a3d71c. All three new PRs have independent complete persistent Git stores/worktrees and private runtime caches; source histories have0missing reachable objects, no alternates/hardlinks/promisor. A preparation clone exposed missing historical objects; accepted upstream history was recovered into owned stores before publication, with no source revision change or actual cross-lane interference. Review scopes are split144/17/24files under the currently documented Essentials150file included limit, with no artifact exclusions, filters or paid overage. Included allowance was last observed0 with no reset; refreshed allowance remains unknown. Native metadata is distinct from requesting reviews.\n\nRelates to https://github.com/open-hax/knoxx/issues/161; closes neither161 nor existing181/182. Native issue hold: https://github.com/open-hax/knoxx/issues/161#issuecomment-6029753221. Missing direct blocker transition is already owned by https://github.com/open-hax/rheos/issues/4 and its personal planningPR3.\n",
